-<h2>Chapter The Optative</h2>
-<p>
- by <span><a class="Contributor" href="https://wals.info/author/dobrushinan" title="Nina Dobrushina">Nina Dobrushina</a> and <a class="Contributor" href="https://wals.info/author/vanderauweraj" title="Johan van der Auwera">Johan van der Auwera</a> and <a class="Contributor" href="https://wals.info/author/goussevv" title="Valentin Goussev">Valentin Goussev</a></span> <button class="btn" id="cite-button-73" onclick="CLLD.Modal.show(&#34;The Optative&#34;, &#34;https://wals.info/chapter/73.md.html&#34;)" type="button">cite</button>
-</p>
-
-<div dir="ltr" id="description">
-<h2 class="heading-1">
-<a name="1._Introduction"></a>1. Introduction</h2>
-<p class="Textbody">In this chapter, the term <i>optative</i> will refer to an inflected verb form dedicated to the expression of <b>the wish of the speaker</b>. An example comes from <a class="Language" href="https://wals.info/languoid/lect/wals_code_bgv" title="view language details">Bagvalal</a> (<a class="Family" href="https://wals.info/languoid/family/nakhdaghestanian" title="Nakh-Daghestanian">Nakh-Daghestanian</a>; eastern Caucasus):</p>
-<blockquote class="example"><p class="example-start">(1) <a class="Language" href="https://wals.info/languoid/lect/wals_code_bgv" title="view language details">Bagvalal</a> (<a class="Reference" href="https://wals.info/refdb/record/Dobrusina-2001" title="view reference details">Dobrušina 2001</a>: 328-329) </p>
