-<p class="Standard">‘Shouldn’t you give me a rupee?’ </p>
-</td>
-</tr>
-</table>
-</div>
-<p class="example-end"></p></blockquote>
-<p class="Textbody">The problem is that there may be an overlap between optatives and imperatives or hortatives in the third person. Third person imperative (hortative) may be used as third person optative and vice versa. Consider the uses of the third person imperative in <a class="Language" href="https://wals.info/languoid/lect/wals_code_map" title="view language details">Mapudungun</a> (<a class="Country" href="https://wals.info/country/CL" title="view languages for country">Chile</a>). A true imperative use is shown in (12a) and a semantically optative one is shown in (12b). </p>
-<blockquote class="example"><p class="example-start">(12) <a class="Language" href="https://wals.info/languoid/lect/wals_code_map" title="view language details">Mapudungun</a> (<a class="Reference" href="https://wals.info/refdb/record/Smeets-1989" title="view reference details">Smeets 1989</a>: 234) </p>
-<div style="text-align:left">
-<table class="table table-hover">
-<tr>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard">a. </p>
-</td>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard"><i>Chewrumé </i></p>
-</td>
-<td colspan="2" style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard"><i>rüngkü-pe! </i></p>
-</td>
-</tr>
-<tr>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-</td>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard">wherever </p>
-</td>
-<td colspan="2" style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard">jump-<span class="T3"><span class="hint--bottom" data-hint="imperative">imp</span></span>.3</p>
-</td>
-</tr>
-<tr>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-</td>
-<td colspan="3" style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard">‘Let him jump wherever he wants to!’ </p>
-</td>
-</tr>
-<tr>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard">b. </p>
-</td>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard"><i>Küme-le-pe </i></p>
-</td>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard"><i>ñi </i></p>
-</td>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-<p class="Standard"><i>fochüm! </i></p>
-</td>
-</tr>
-<tr>
-<td style="text-align:left;">
-</td>
